WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.630
For the Ritual,

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.640
a sacrifice is required.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.520
-A sacrifice?
-Why are you surprised?

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.140
This is the country's priority.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:16.400
Giving a sacrifice to step into god's
domain is common throughout the world.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.980
Your job was to guide him to Fushido
and roll him to sleep.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.860
The duties thereafter are all entrusted
to the Key Girl.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:23.780
Key Girl?

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.490
The one offered to sleep
in the Fushido of Lord Mitatsu.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.950
Literally, she is a living key to remain
married to him until her life is depleted.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.870
My God...

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:38.460
no matter how conceited she is,
sacrificing her goes too far!

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:44.090
Those girls were born for Lord Mitatsu's
use and understand more than anyone.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.970
Offering one's life to Lord Mitatsu
as the Key Girl

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:53.270
is the greatest honor for a miko.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:04.490
<i>I have been waiting for this day.</i>

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:13.870
<i>Always waiting...</i>

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:15.790
<i>for today.</i>

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:21.380
And they say that the Key Girl and
Lord Mitatsu become one for all eternity!

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.880
That moment's supposed to feel amazing.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.380
Seriously? Even more than that?

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:29.050
-More than what?
-Natsume, you're so out of it.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.100
They're talking about sex.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.010
Get it?

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:36.850
Natsume.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.230
Haru.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.400
<i>I am the Key Girl.</i>

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.700
<i>I will drive the key into Lord Mitatsu</i>

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.200
<i>and pledge myself to him</i>

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:52.240
<i>for eternity.</i>

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:13.180
She was chosen to be the Key Girl.

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.060
I wanted to save her.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.560
I didn't care about the country
or the Ritual,

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:22.230
just... her.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.900
We planned on escaping during the Ritual.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:33.330
Riding away on Montparnasse... on Masotan.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:34.870
Montparnasse...

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.040
However...

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.830
Lord Mitatsu was a step ahead of us.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.420
He understood the gravity of our actions.

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:48.380
Sada... I can't go after all.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.760
You promised we would run away together!

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.640
You said we'd go to Paris!

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:57.270
If I didn't become the Key Girl,

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.690
The country would be finished.

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.610
Many people would disappear.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.650
You, my parents...

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.280
-But...
-I was so glad...

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:11.530
to have met you.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.780
If I close my eyes, I can float.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:19.460
Look at our beloved Montparnasse.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.330
Yae...

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:33.800
Yae!

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:38.520
If this is the last view I see,

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.020
then I am happy.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.190
Yae!

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.900
People betray one another.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:52.530
Yes.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:54.910
I betrayed Yae.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:59.620
But I will no longer betray anyone.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:04.630
I resolved to give everything I have
to Montparnasse.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:10.420
But... Montparnasse rejected me.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:13.430
It's no surprise.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:18.560
I never wished to become one
with Montparnasse.

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:25.850
This time, I will definitively finish the
Ritual that Yae gave her life for.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:31.860
That is my only wish.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.360
What should we do?

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:37.320
We didn't hear anything about a sacrifice!

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:42.120
I can't even think of someone
being sacrificed... I just can't!

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.580
But if the Key Girl doesn't succeed...

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:48.420
Then we'll all be doomed to die
with the submergence of Japan.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.340
I wonder if we can get
everyone to find shelter...

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.010
Technical Sergeant Amakasu.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:54.380
Yes?

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:58.220
Between someone I cherished
and the Ritual,

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:01.220
I couldn't choose either
and was left in limbo.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:06.600
But you... chose both.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.860
On top of that, you flew.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.690
I want to ask you this...

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.450
Hisone Amakasu, in this situation,

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.580
which future would you choose?

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:40.680
<i>She's back.</i>

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:43.180
<i>Amakasu came back.</i>

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:48.150
<i>I was convinced...</i>

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:52.900
<i>that things were just the way they were.</i>

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.320
<i>But...</i>

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:00.320
<i>what other people accept as normal</i>

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.410
<i>are things that I fret and struggle over.</i>

00:06:05.450 --> 00:06:10.330
<i>When I saw that Amakasu searched</i>
<i>for answers that were only right for her,</i>

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.380
<i>I realized that maybe...</i>

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:16.050
<i>there is no normal to be found.</i>

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:26.350
Amakasu,

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.940
If you were me, what would you say?

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:30.690
I will prevent it!

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.900
I cannot stand by and watch someone die!

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:36.820
We're still members
of the Air Self-Defense Force!

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.700
Then the country will--

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:39.910
No, it won't!

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:41.410
She can't think clearly.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.120
I can think!
I'm thinking at full throttle!

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:47.700
Aside from the sacrifice, we've only
recently found out about the Ritual!

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:50.710
If we discussed it together, then maybe
we could've found a way out!

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:52.750
But this has been going on for years--

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.250
Who decided that?

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:57.840
What time? What minute? What second?
How many revolutions of the earth?

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.470
-Wow, she's like a child.
-Yes, she is.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.560
The large-scale OTF's activity has
yet to resume.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:08.850
It'll soon be two hours.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:11.190
If he isn't rolled to sleep...

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:12.900
What are those girls doing?!

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:15.690
Telemetry signal from an OTF is confirmed!

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:16.860
Finally!

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:19.190
But the activation is coming

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:20.820
only from one aircraft!

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:39.920
<i>I wonder why?</i>

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.140
<i>Haru and I...</i>

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:46.180
<i>have lived for this day.</i>

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:49.930
<i>But...</i>

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.360
<i>it doesn't feel good at all.</i>

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:05.950
Natsu--

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.670
Amakasu?

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.300
Don't do it, Natsume!

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:23.340
Sacrificing yourself is crazy!

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:25.010
Get out of here!

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:27.890
How far will you go to interfere?
It's annoying!

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:30.270
I've waited my whole life for this day.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.480
It was the same for us too, you know.

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:35.900
For Haru and me, this is the climax.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:38.820
There's not even a hair's width
of space for you here.

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:45.160
Then you're a cheater,
aren't you, Natsume?

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:49.200
You're going to be married for life
to Lord Mitatsu, right?

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:52.750
Isn't that a weird climax
to share with Okonogi?

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.500
That is an illicit sexual affair!

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:55.870
Well that's the way it goes!

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:57.040
In that case,

00:08:57.170 --> 00:09:01.090
the epilogue will be a new world
for me and Haru!

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:02.670
Haru?

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:05.050
Because I like Haru!

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.180
And it's a purer,
purer feeling than yours!

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:13.680
Once you're gone, I'll be enjoying
my first love Haru to the very fullest!

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:15.440
He's my first love!

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:18.940
-And I've liked him since I was a kid!
-Calm down, you two!

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:21.900
I've never liked another boy
and matured for my first love...

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:25.070
-How long will this go on?
-Who knows?

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:25.990
Who needs that?!

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:27.950
Once you're gone,

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:31.870
Haru and I will
instantly start making out!

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:33.910
-Of course you won't!
-In that case...

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.000
live!

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:42.250
Fight with me over Haru!

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:45.380
A fair and square fight for love!

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:48.010
I've never competed with anyone before.

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:52.890
But I can have
a refreshing battle with you, Natsume!

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:58.230
Amakasu.

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:01.570
Oh no!

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:03.150
Lord Mitatsu is...

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:12.160
The large-scale OTF has begun
to sink in elevation.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:13.950
-Is it being rolled to sleep?
-Unknown.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:15.700
Currently at 1500 feet.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:16.870
Still falling in elevation.

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:21.630
They didn't put him to sleep.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:25.300
This is the end of the Ritual.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:26.760
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:31.430
There is no time left to put
Lord Mitatsu to sleep.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.970
We will roll in him into sleep like this.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:39.560
Hiso Maso!

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:47.440
Normally, the Ritual lures Lord Mitatsu
to sleep and then we roll him over.

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:51.620
Then, the Key Girl's prayer
would stabilize the land.

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:54.950
However, this time
we won't lure him to sleep,

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:57.200
and force him to roll over.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.160
What after that?

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:01.040
<i>We'll figure it out as we go along.</i>

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:02.290
Quit taking liberties!

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:04.670
<i>This is in the realm of the Dragon Pilots!</i>

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:09.680
No matter what order you give from
your safe place, we're the ones doing it!

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:13.760
If you want to talk the talk,
then come here and walk the walk.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:16.680
<i>Everyone!</i>

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:19.810
-Hitomin!
-<i>There's been a change of plans.</i>

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:23.810
<i>We are going to force</i>
<i>Lord Mitatsu to roll over!</i>

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:29.190
<i>Everyone, please evacuate</i>
<i>to the transport module for now!</i>

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:33.620
That's impossible! Even if you succeed,
without a Key Girl, Lord Mitatsu will--

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:36.120
-Yeah. Hurry up!
-That hurts!

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:46.420
I'm here!

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:48.760
Get to the rendezvous point quickly!

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:52.430
-<i>Yes, ma'am!</i>
-I'll direct from the transport module.

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:55.430
Hisone Amakasu, I want you to show me

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:57.970
<i>the skies you choose!</i>

00:11:58.850 --> 00:11:59.680
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:03.560
<i>To the Yokota COC. This is Shenron.</i>

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:06.150
<i>We will begin the rolling now.</i>

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.070
<i>Roger.</i>

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:10.900
<i>Your target is the Shimenawa rope</i>
<i>made of his tails tied together.</i>

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.910
<i>Once you shoot the harpoon,</i>
<i>there is no do-over!</i>

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:16.410
<i>Do it as carefully</i>
<i>and quickly as possible!</i>

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:17.530
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:37.220
<i>Wyvern has dropped the pod!</i>

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:40.770
<i>Send the F patrolling the area that way,</i>
<i>or at least an AAM!</i>

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:43.230
The large-scale OTF is
at the center of the storm area.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:45.270
We cannot get close.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:47.060
<i>New contact. It's Serpent!</i>

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:50.780
Sorry for the wait!

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:53.820
Masotan!

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:56.990
They're going to take on Lord Mitatsu...

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:58.450
They can't possibly do it.

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:05.170
Masotan and I are betting
everything on this one shot!

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:12.960
<i>You blockhead!</i>

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:14.760
No, there's still a chance!

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:16.180
<i>But the harpoon--</i>

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:18.850
We have Masotan and the others!

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:24.480
Masotan!

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:47.460
<i>You lead the timing! Let's do it together!</i>

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.540
-But...
-<i>It's worth trying!</i>

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:50.630
Okay!

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:55.550
Go! All the way to the limit!

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:04.060
They did it!

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:05.480
We did it!

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:08.060
That girl's impressive.

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:10.560
Yeah, she is.

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:14.570
Those girls found it.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:17.280
<i>They live...</i>

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:19.660
<i>and they found it...</i>

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:22.240
<i>the thing they cherish.</i>

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:25.410
<i>That's why they're strong.</i>

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:26.910
<i>Always...</i>

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:30.670
I...

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:32.710
haven't...

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:35.300
found mine yet.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:37.880
-Natsume.
-I haven't found it.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:39.760
Nothing yet.

00:14:42.050 --> 00:14:42.930
I...

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:46.270
don't want to die!

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:50.230
Yeah.

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:53.570
Let's live, Natsume.

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:03.200
Do it now, Key Girl!

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:06.450
Pierce the bell staff straight
into Lord Mitatsu's heart!

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.210
With it wedged into the axis of rotation,

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:11.040
it will stop the rolling!

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:12.420
However,

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:17.380
blocking the axis means
she cannot return to us.

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:20.630
It's a physical thing?

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:23.470
<i>Then that means anyone can do it,</i>
<i>not just the Key Girl!</i>

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:27.520
<i>Which means a sacrifice is</i>
<i>necessary either way.</i>

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:32.900
Can you let me do it?

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:34.610
Haru?

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:37.190
I'll wedge the key inside
instead of Natsume!

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:39.190
Wait, Haru! The bell staff is--

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:40.150
It's okay.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:42.530
-I can't let you--
-That's not it.

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:45.870
I dropped the bell staff.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:47.290
Oh my God!

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:48.950
We're out of options...

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:52.920
<i>Excuse me for jumping in the middle.</i>

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:54.380
Amakasu?

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:56.420
<i>I'll be right back.</i>

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:58.960
What are you saying, Amakasu?

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:01.470
It just seemed like
we weren't getting anywhere...

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:04.680
<i>And I recovered the bell staff,</i>
<i>so no worries!</i>

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:06.470
Don't do it, Amakasu!

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:07.760
Why you!

00:16:07.890 --> 00:16:10.480
<i>Dealing with issues doesn't</i>
<i>exclude danger!</i>

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:12.810
My body is for carrying out my duties,

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:15.520
and with it I vow to take charge
for the citizens of our nation!

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:18.610
-Wait, Technical Sergeant Amakasu!
-I am a Dragon Pilot.

00:16:18.690 --> 00:16:19.530
An ASDF official!

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:22.990
-I will fulfill my duty without fail...
-You can't!

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:24.570
And I will definitely

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:26.030
come back alive!

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:27.280
Amakasu!

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:31.710
<i>Salamander has deployed.</i>

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:35.630
No...

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:38.130
That idiot!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:45.180
That must be it.

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:49.850
Masotan, once I land,
you need to run, too.

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:51.140
Understand?

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:56.770
Masotan, eject!

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:14.410
One, two,

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:23.550
Hot, hot, hot!

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:25.300
Now is the Ritual over?

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:27.890
Masotan?

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:33.180
What are you doing? Hurry up and leave!

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:36.140
Why? You can't, Masotan!

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:38.900
I want to protect you, too!

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:43.990
Everyone is important to me,
but you're especially important!

00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:50.910
Am I possibly...

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:54.040
a special, cherished person to you, too?

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:00.920
That's foolish, Masotan. Foolish!

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:07.510
I love you!

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:53.810
What're you gonna do next?

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:57.060
I've never thought of anything
outside of being a miko.

00:18:57.140 --> 00:18:58.060
We'll waste away.

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.600
Look for an eternal job?

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:02.520
That's impossible for you.

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:05.480
I know. I'll be a florist.

00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:08.240
I was thinking

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:11.610
the blooms would be nice.
The pretty flowers...

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:14.950
in our future.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:21.370
With the end of Gifu's
mixed formation squad,

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:25.880
today also marks the dissolution
of the Special OTF Flight Division.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:29.050
I'm going to miss everyone.

00:19:29.510 --> 00:19:31.630
You're leaving tomorrow morning, right?

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:34.640
What souvenirs should I buy?

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:36.060
Hey, Onaga.

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:39.390
Shouldn't you ask her for her number?

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.810
What are you...

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:43.770
Aren't you going to tell him?

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:46.940
Only if I'm asked directly.

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:48.940
You like to hang them out to dry,
don't you?

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:53.660
What about you, Lilikos? Not going to
exchange numbers with anyone?

00:19:53.740 --> 00:19:56.490
I guess I would for "Kingdom."

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:57.700
Kingdom?

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:00.960
I heard.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.920
That your extremely rude comments

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:08.210
were all said to avoid anastomosis.

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:10.590
You're going back to Tsuiki, right?

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:11.510
Yeah.

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:14.390
Sorry, but I'm kind of...

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:16.970
I don't mind being friends with benefits.

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:20.890
How can you say that, Hoshino?

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:23.980
-Isn't that what you wanted?
-Hell no.

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:25.900
Then what do you want to do?

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:28.570
I want to cherish you.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:38.370
I'll think about it.

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:44.750
Hell yeah!

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.500
Hey, calm down, will ya?

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:52.010
Your stomach will be flying low
if you stuff yourself!

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:53.630
Kaizaki.

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:55.260
Mr. Ikushima!

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:57.510
You look like a true maintenance crewman.

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:59.850
Yes, thanks to you.

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:01.270
About that,

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.890
could you give it another thought?

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:07.810
As a result of creating
a junior size for you,

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:10.610
Brand new possibilities have sprouted up.

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:11.780
Suits for kids--

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:13.860
I most certainly will not think it over.

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:19.160
I've completely become an old person.

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:20.870
You're as youthful as ever.

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:25.920
To this lazy man that I am,

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:28.330
will you sell a Joie?

00:21:30.340 --> 00:21:33.010
Sure. One million yen please.

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:37.090
Ha, ha, you must have grown up in Kansai!

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:38.260
No.

00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:40.890
It's really one million yen.

00:21:40.970 --> 00:21:41.810
Oh my God.

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:44.640
Doesn't it feel too heartless?

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:46.190
What is?

00:21:46.270 --> 00:21:49.230
Taking lightly
the loss of one of our subordinates.

00:21:49.360 --> 00:21:52.360
Commander Sosoda, Flight Leader Kakiyasu,

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:55.530
and all the Dragon Pilots act
like business as usual.

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:58.870
Maezawa has been reading
Buddhist sutras every morning.

00:21:58.950 --> 00:21:59.780
Shut up!

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:01.910
Thank you.

00:22:02.370 --> 00:22:03.870
But we'll be fine.

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:06.000
She is definitely...

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:07.920
Hey!

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:11.540
She's not coming home. How irresponsible.

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:15.470
I wanted to chat with her
before heading back to Iruma.

00:22:15.550 --> 00:22:17.880
But it's been three months.

00:22:17.970 --> 00:22:19.800
I'm getting a little worried.

00:22:20.260 --> 00:22:22.260
Well, something'll work out.

00:22:22.640 --> 00:22:25.560
As long as she's got Masotan,
she's invincible.

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:27.770
-Yeah!
-That's true.

00:22:27.940 --> 00:22:28.940
She's invincible.

00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:31.560
Even so, there's a least one person

00:22:31.940 --> 00:22:34.530
who can't sit still waiting.

00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:38.570
<i>National Land Afforestation Promotion</i>
<i>Organization and Toyama Prefecture</i>

00:22:38.780 --> 00:22:41.570
will hold on the ninth at Mount Arimine

00:22:41.870 --> 00:22:45.410
<i>the 71st National Arbor Day.</i>

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:47.370
<i>The prefecture's Arbor Day began in 1971,</i>

00:22:47.460 --> 00:22:52.420
<i>and will be held here</i>
<i>for the second time in 47 years.</i>

00:22:52.840 --> 00:22:56.260
<i>Due to the bomb cyclone</i>
<i>on Mount Arimine back in March,</i>

00:22:56.340 --> 00:23:00.050
<i>major landslides struck the region</i>
<i>during rainstorms.</i>

00:23:00.180 --> 00:23:04.260
<i>Prefectural Governor Hyoue Yoshizawa</i>
<i>began a forestry recycling initiative--</i>

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:11.230
According to the report immediately after,
in the land where Lord Mitatsu burrowed,

00:23:11.310 --> 00:23:13.520
Masotan's telemetry could not be found.

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:16.860
I bought these for you.

00:23:17.110 --> 00:23:18.530
I burned through my savings.

00:23:19.360 --> 00:23:21.410
<i>But... they're definitely okay.</i>

00:23:22.530 --> 00:23:24.780
<i>For someone who only says the truth,</i>

00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:27.040
<i>if she says she'll come home alive,</i>
<i>she will.</i>

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:31.290
<i>Besides, it's a bit of a relief</i>

00:23:32.330 --> 00:23:34.790
<i>that he is by her self.</i>

00:23:49.140 --> 00:23:50.980
Okonog?

00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:52.600
Amakasu?

00:23:52.730 --> 00:23:55.060
What are you doing here?

00:23:55.150 --> 00:23:57.070
That's what I want to know!

00:23:57.150 --> 00:23:59.240
-Where have you been?
-It's so good to see you!

00:23:59.320 --> 00:24:00.950
Have you been well?

00:24:02.360 --> 00:24:03.450
Yup. I'm doing well.

00:24:03.530 --> 00:24:05.450
Wait, no I'm not! Amakasu!

00:24:09.950 --> 00:24:12.790
<i>Because we're invincible,</i>

00:24:13.750 --> 00:24:17.630
<i>we'll find many more things to cherish!</i>

00:24:17.710 --> 00:24:21.970
THE END
